muructl
=======

a minimal command-line service control utility for Linux


HOW TO COMPILE
==============

run "make"

to install, use "make install"

if you want to install to a different root directory, define DESTDIR
as your desired prefix.


DESCRIPTION
===========

muructl is a minimal command-line utility for managing services
through a Unix domain socket.

It provides a simple interface for controlling services, with a
focus on simplicity and minimal dependencies.


COMMANDS
========

usage: muructl <command> [service]

commands:
  start NAME      Start service
  stop NAME       Stop service
  restart NAME    Restart service
  status NAME     Show service status
  list            List services


REQUIREMENTS
============

muructl requires root privileges to run.

The service control daemon must be running and listening on the
configured Unix domain socket.

Before starting a service, its service definition must exist in
the configured services directory.


DESIGN
======

muructl aims to keep its implementation small, straightforward,
and easy to maintain.